WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.113
One point two five billion dollars in total political contributions, tracked from 2004 to the present.

00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:08.863
Every dollar from Elections Canada's open data.

00:00:08.863 --> 00:00:10.363
Ten major parties.

00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:12.147
Party-by-party allocation.

00:00:12.147 --> 00:00:13.715
Year-over-year trends.

00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:17.261
The dashboard breaks down who gave how much to whom, and when.

00:00:17.261 --> 00:00:18.261
Liberal red.

00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:19.545
Conservative blue.

00:00:19.545 --> 00:00:20.852
NDP orange.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:21.636
Green.

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:28.852
Every colour on the chart represents real money from real donors — and the patterns show which parties benefit from which economic conditions.

00:00:28.852 --> 00:00:30.465
This is not analysis.

00:00:30.465 --> 00:00:31.947
This is arithmetic.

00:00:31.947 --> 00:00:33.499
The government published the data.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.704
We added it up.

00:00:34.704 --> 00:00:36.829
The pie charts show allocation.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:38.613
The bar charts show trends.

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:40.431
The tables show details.

00:00:40.431 --> 00:00:42.113
Draw your own conclusions.
